# Sonata project board (Notion)

Tracking lives in **Notion**, not Linear. Full workflow: `AGENTS.md` and
`.agents/rules/project-manager-guide.md`.

- **Project:** https://app.notion.com/p/39d243549f638012be2bca1294ec5c79
- **SONA Tickets:** https://app.notion.com/p/ba5243549f63822db8f9019f8d89beb6
- **Data source:** `collection://fe024354-9f63-83db-87dc-07f92799408c`
- **Page templates** (prefer when creating tickets):

| Type | Template | `template_id` |
|------|----------|---------------|
| `Story` | Feature Ticket | `bd624354-9f63-8237-99c9-015f6ae2a183` |
| `Bug` | Bug Ticket | `f5024354-9f63-821a-ad85-81550fdbc659` |
| `Spike` | Spike Ticket | `fad24354-9f63-839c-aa6d-01f45e181907` |
| `Task` | Task Ticket | `71824354-9f63-8334-8649-01a2c41e7e0b` |
| `Plan` | Dev Plan | `65724354-9f63-8382-8898-810fd27b31e7` |
| `Task` | Test Request | `3c424354-9f63-8060-aaca-c259a8d45cff` |

- Details: `.agents/notion-templates.md`
- IDs: `SONA-{n}` (Notion auto-increment `ID`)
- After create, set ticket **Name** to `SONA-{n}: {title}` so Notion
  search works. Skip Test Requests (`TR: …`) and Dev Plans.
- Statuses: `New` → `Planning` → `Ready` → `In progress` → `In Review` → `Done`
- Dev Plans: child pages with `Type=Plan` + `Parent` relation
- Feature PRs target **`testing`** (squash-merge as `SONA-{n}: Title` + bullets). `master` only via a `TR:` PR after QA.
- Test Request template: only if the user confirms. Use the `test-request` skill.
- Use Notion MCP for create/query/update; do not create Linear issues
